+**Match the response to the size of the problem.** Before acting on anything that went wrong, decide which it is:
+
+- **A single event**: one failure, one outage, one stale line, one slow review. Apply the routine consequence above and nothing more.
+- **A pattern**: the same problem twice or more, across tasks or producers. Send it to the diagnostician.
+- **A break**: a misreport, a constraint break, or a threat to the goal or budget. Only these justify stopping work, changing anything swarm-wide, or escalating to the human.
+
+Over-reacting costs as much as under-reacting. It spends review and budget, stops progress, and teaches the swarm that reporting a small problem is risky. A one-off failure by a reliable producer is the schedule working, not a signal to tighten everything.
